{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return an ordered list of prime factors for a given integer n, including multiplicity.\n    The product of the factors equals the original input n.\n    \"\"\"\n    factors = []\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return factors\n\n    # Factor out 2s\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        factors.append(2)\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Factor out odd numbers\n    d = 3\n    while d * d <= n:\n        while n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            n //= d\n        d += 2\n\n    # Handle remaining prime factor\n    if n > 1:\n        factors.append(n)\n\n    return factors"}
