{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' where elements at indices not divisible by three are preserved, and elements at indices divisible by three are sorted.\n    The input list l is not mutated.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    l_prime = [None] * n\n    collected_values = []\n\n    # First pass: Collect values at divisible-by-three indices and copy others\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            collected_values.append(l[i])\n        else:\n            l_prime[i] = l[i]\n\n    # Sort the collected values\n    collected_values.sort()\n\n    # Second pass: Place the sorted values back into l' at their original divisible-by-three indices\n    sorted_idx = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            l_prime[i] = collected_values[sorted_idx]\n            sorted_idx += 1\n\n    return l_prime"}
