{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "def sort_even(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    l_prime = [None] * n\n\n    even_indexed_values = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            even_indexed_values.append(l[i])\n\n    even_indexed_values.sort()\n\n    even_ptr = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 2 == 1:\n            l_prime[i] = l[i]\n        else:\n            l_prime[i] = even_indexed_values[even_ptr]\n            even_ptr += 1\n\n    return l_prime"}
