{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize with the base case values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    # 'last_four' will always store [fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1)] for the current iteration i.\n    last_four = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        # Calculate the next fib4 number using the sum of the last four values.\n        next_fib4 = last_four[3] + last_four[2] + last_four[1] + last_four[0]\n        # Shift the window to keep only the last four relevant values.\n        last_four[0] = last_four[1]\n        last_four[1] = last_four[2]\n        last_four[2] = last_four[3]\n        last_four[3] = next_fib4\n\n    return last_four[3]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence efficiently without recursion.\n    The sequence is defined by fib4(0)=0, fib4(1)=0, fib4(2)=2, fib4(3)=0, and fib4(n) = fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4) for n > 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    _cache = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = _cache[i-1] + _cache[i-2] + _cache[i-3] + _cache[i-4]\n        _cache.append(next_fib4)\n\n    return _cache[n]"}
