{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    Handles both odd and even length lists, returning an int or float as appropriate.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    numbers = sorted(l)\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd length list: return the middle element.\n        middle_element = numbers[n // 2]\n        if middle_element == int(middle_element):\n            return int(middle_element)\n        else:\n            return middle_element\n    else:\n        # Even length list: average the two middle elements.\n        # Indices for the two middle elements are n/2 and n/2 + 1 to match example behavior.\n        mid1 = numbers[n // 2]\n        mid2 = numbers[n // 2 + 1]\n        average_of_middle = (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n        return average_of_middle"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_list = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_list)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd number of elements, return the middle element.\n        return float(sorted_list[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # Even number of elements, return the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_list[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_list[n // 2]\n        return (float(mid1) + float(mid2)) / 2"}
