{"task_id": "HumanEval/108", "solution": "def _calculate_sum_of_digits(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of digits for a number, handling negative first digits.\"\"\"\n    s_num = str(num)\n    digit_sum = 0\n\n    if num < 0:\n        # The first digit after '-' is treated as negative.\n        digit_sum -= int(s_num[1])\n        # Add remaining digits as positive.\n        for digit_char in s_num[2:]:\n            digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n    else:\n        # For non-negative numbers, sum all digits as positive.\n        for digit_char in s_num:\n            digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n    return digit_sum\ndef count_nums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts numbers in an array where the sum of digits is greater than 0.\n    For negative numbers, the first digit is treated as negative (e.g., -123 has digits -1, 2, 3).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if not arr:  # Handles the empty array case directly.\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    for num in arr:\n        current_sum = _calculate_sum_of_digits(num)\n        if current_sum > 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/107", "solution": "def _is_palindrome(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an integer is a palindrome by comparing its string representation with its reverse.\"\"\"\n    s = str(num)\n    return s == s[::-1]\ndef _is_even(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an integer is even using the modulo operator.\"\"\"\n    return num % 2 == 0\ndef even_odd_palindrome(n: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Counts even and odd integer palindromes in the range [1, n].\"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if _is_palindrome(i):\n            if _is_even(i):\n                even_count += 1\n            else:\n                odd_count += 1\n    return (even_count, odd_count)"}
