{"task_id": "HumanEval/117", "solution": "def select_words(s, n):\n    \"\"\"Given a string s and a natural number n, return a list of words with exactly n consonants.\n    Words are returned in their original order; an empty string yields an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_vowel(char):\n        \"\"\"Determines if a character is a vowel (a, e, i, o, u, case-insensitive).\"\"\"\n        return char.lower() in 'aeiou'\n\n    def _is_consonant(char):\n        \"\"\"Determines if a character is a consonant (any letter not an 'aeiou' vowel, including 'y').\"\"\"\n        return char.isalpha() and not _is_vowel(char)\n\n    if not s:\n        return []\n\n    result_words = []\n    words = s.split()\n\n    for word_str in words:\n        consonant_count = 0\n        for char in word_str:\n            if _is_consonant(char):\n                consonant_count += 1\n\n        if consonant_count == n:\n            result_words.append(word_str)\n\n    return result_words"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/116", "solution": "def _count_set_bits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of set bits (ones) in an integer's binary representation.\n    It considers the absolute value for bit counting.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    return bin(abs(n)).count('1')\ndef sort_array(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    In this Kata, you have to sort an array of non-negative integers according to\n    number of ones in their binary representation in ascending order.\n    For similar number of ones, sort based on decimal value.\n\n    It must be implemented like this:\n    >>> sort_array([1, 5, 2, 3, 4]) == [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n    >>> sort_array([-2, -3, -4, -5, -6]) == [-6, -5, -4, -3, -2]\n    >>> sort_array([1, 0, 2, 3, 4]) [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    return sorted(arr, key=lambda x: (_count_set_bits(x), x))"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/110", "solution": "def is_even(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is even.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 == 0\ndef count_odd_numbers(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of odd integers in a list.\"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        if not is_even(number):\n            odd_count += 1\n    return odd_count\ndef count_even_numbers(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of even integers in a list.\"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        if is_even(number):\n            even_count += 1\n    return even_count\ndef exchange(lst1: list[int], lst2: list[int]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"In this problem, you will implement a function that takes two lists of numbers,\n    and determines whether it is possible to perform an exchange of elements\n    between them to make lst1 a list of only even numbers.\n    There is no limit on the number of exchanged elements between lst1 and lst2.\n    If it is possible to exchange elements between the lst1 and lst2 to make\n    all the elements of lst1 to be even, return \"YES\".\n    Otherwise, return \"NO\".\n    For example:\n    exchange([1, 2, 3, 4], [1, 2, 3, 4]) => \"YES\"\n    exchange([1, 2, 3, 4], [1, 5, 3, 4]) => \"NO\"\n    It is assumed that the input lists will be non-empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_in_lst1_count = count_odd_numbers(lst1)\n    even_in_lst2_count = count_even_numbers(lst2)\n\n    if even_in_lst2_count >= odd_in_lst1_count:\n        return \"YES\"\n    else:\n        return \"NO\""}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/117", "solution": "def _is_consonant(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given character is a consonant.\"\"\"\n    char_lower = char.lower()\n    return char_lower.isalpha() and char_lower not in 'aeiou'\ndef _count_consonants(word: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of consonants in a word.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for char in word:\n        if _is_consonant(char):\n            count += 1\n    return count\ndef select_words(s: str, n: int) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string s and a natural number n, this function returns a list of all words from string s\n    that contain exactly n consonants, in order these words appear in the string s.\n    If the string s is empty then the function should return an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return []\n\n    result_words = []\n    words = s.split()\n\n    for word in words:\n        if _count_consonants(word) == n:\n            result_words.append(word)\n\n    return result_words"}
